<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Geronimo returns six weeks after intake, with the interpreter. He has had four sessions of cognitive processing therapy and says the therapist listens and does not push him to speak of what he will not. He drinks on two evenings a week, two drinks each time, and has had no nausea on naltrexone. The nightmares still come about four nights a week and he sleeps four or five hours. He asks whether a medicine could help him sleep and lift the heaviness. Sertraline was explained, with its side effects and the sodium check, and prazosin for nightmares was discussed: he chose sertraline at a low dose and agreed to wait on prazosin because of his fall. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>Four of twelve sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Drinking</td><td>Two evenings a week, two drinks each</td></tr><tr><td>PCL-5</td><td>46</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>10, item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Liver tests</td><td>AST 41, ALT 31, GGT 84 U/L</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

